# tools/box-runner/box-runner.env -- supervisor configuration.
#
# Copy this file to box-runner.env next to supervisor.sh (install.sh does
# this for you, without overwriting an existing one) and edit it in place.
# Keep it root:wheel 0644 -- NO secrets belong in this file. The only durable
# secret in this whole system is the GitHub App private key, and even that
# lives OUTSIDE this repo entirely: only its path (GH_APP_KEY, read by
# gh-app-mint.sh, itself invoked from here only by path via GH_APP_MINT) is
# configured anywhere in this tree. See gh-app-mint.sh's own header for its
# required env (GH_APP_ID / GH_APP_KEY / GH_RUNNER_REPO) -- set those either
# by exporting them wherever this box starts supervisor.sh (the launchd
# plist's EnvironmentVariables, e.g.), or by pointing BOX_RUNNER_APP_ENV at a
# second, more tightly permissioned file that gh-app-mint.sh sources before
# checking them. This file does not set any of the three.

# --- Required: no default, supervisor.sh refuses to start without these -----

# Path to the actions-runner install (see install.sh), owned by RUNNER_USER.
RUNNER_DIR=/Users/runner/actions-runner

# Labels this runner's JIT registration advertises. MUST match (a subset of)
# the `runs-on:` list in .github/workflows/benchmark.yml, which is
# `[self-hosted, Linux, ARM64, qwen3.8-125b-a6b-cuda-v1]` (the GB10 box).
# GitHub does NOT auto-add self-hosted/OS/arch to a JIT-registered runner the
# way config.sh runners get them for free; gh-app-mint.sh force-includes
# "self-hosted" itself, but every further label the workflow's runs-on requires
# must be listed here, comma-separated. A wrong value here does not fail loudly
# -- it silently strands every dispatched job with no runner willing to pick it
# up.
#
# NOTE: this supervisor, install.sh and the plist are the macOS/launchd
# lineage. The GB10 box is Linux, so registering a runner there needs a
# Linux/systemd port of tools/box-runner/ (a separate box-ops lane). The label
# set below is the ranked workflow's, kept in step with its runs-on regardless.
#
# The last label IS the track id (= the branch name = the R2 key prefix), so it
# changes only when the track does. Linux and ARM64 name the box. For that
# workflow as it stands:
#
#   RUNNER_LABELS=Linux,ARM64,qwen3.8-125b-a6b-cuda-v1
#
# It is left EMPTY below, and supervisor.sh refuses to start (exit 78) while it
# stays empty, so seeding this file on a box is never the same act as putting
# that box into a track's ranked rotation.
RUNNER_LABELS=

# --- Optional (defaults shown are supervisor.sh's built-in ones) -----------

RUNNER_USER=runner
GH_APP_MINT=./gh-app-mint.sh
RUNNER_NAME_PREFIX=qwen38-125b-a6b-box
LOG_DIR=./log
STATE_DIR=./state

# Seconds to wait between jobs, and how long an idle JIT registration lives
# before being recycled (requires GNU `timeout`/`gtimeout` on PATH; skipped,
# not fatal, when absent).
PAUSE_BETWEEN_JOBS=15
IDLE_RECYCLE_SECONDS=3600

# Grace period between SIGTERM and SIGKILL when stopping a job's process
# tree (supervisor.sh stop, and the between-jobs/startup reap).
STOP_TERM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=10

# Optional operator alert hook: an executable called with one message
# argument on mint failure or an incomplete stop. Must never itself fail;
# supervisor.sh already logs to LOG_DIR/supervisor.log regardless of whether
# this is set.
ALERT_HOOK=

# --- TEST/DRY-RUN ONLY -- do not set either of these in this file on a real
# box. They exist so tools/box-runner/test/test-box-runner.sh can exercise
# the spawn/stop/status/kill-tree logic without root or a provisioned
# `runner` account. install.sh never writes them here.
#   RUNNER_SU_ENABLED=0
#   BOX_RUNNER_MAX_ITERATIONS=1
